'''Najra-Va''' was a rocky [[planet]] in the [[Dassal system]] of the [[Unknown Regions]], [[orbit]]ed by a once-inhabited [[Unidentified moon (Najra-Va)|moon]]. Along with the other celestial bodies in the [[Star system|system]], Najra-Va was cored out by the [[First Order]] as a test for the [[Starkiller Base]] [[superweapon]] in the [[Standard year|year]] [[34 ABY]]. However, unlike the other worlds, Najra-Va remained mostly intact after the tests, albeit with a core shaft straight through the planet's center. The [[Resistance pilot]]s [[Kazuda Xiono]] and [[Poe Dameron]] flew through the planet's core shaft while [[Mission to the Dassal system|investigating]] the First Order's presence in the system.

==Description==
{{Quote|What is that? Poe?''"<br />"''Yeah, I see it. It's a gravity well.|Kazuda Xiono and Poe Dameron|audio=PoeGravityWell-TheCoreProblem.flac|<ref name="The Core Problem" />}}
[[File:Dassal-Demir-Tehar-GalaxyMap.png|thumb|right|270px|The Dassal system, home of Najra-Va, was located in the Unknown Regions.]]
A rocky terrestrial [[planet]]<ref name="BSOTEAFO">{{EncyclopediaCite|Battle Stations of the Empire and the First Order}}</ref> [[orbit]]ed by a formerly-inhabited [[Unidentified moon (Najra-Va)|moon]],<ref name="The Core Problem" /> Najra-Va was located in the [[Unknown Regions]]'s [[Dassal system]], within [[Sector Epsilon 51-3]]<ref name="BSOTEAFO" /> in grid square H-7 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Grid Coordinates" /> After the militant [[First Order]] cored out the planets in the [[Star system|system]],<ref name="Resistance Rewind">{{SWYouTube|series=Resistance Rewind|text=#1.18: The First Order's Plan|video=1q-4qXOa5F0|sw_url=video/disneyxd-the-first-order-s-plan-resistance-rewind}}</ref> Najra-Va was left with a circular tunnel that covered its entire diameter,<ref name="The Core Problem" /> and all of the planet's inhabitants and ecosystems perished.<ref name="BSOTEAFO" /> Despite no longer having matter in its core, a [[gravity well]] still existed in the center of the planet.<ref name="The Core Problem" /> Najra-Va orbited a single [[Dassal system's sun|sun]], which disappeared due to the First Order's experiments. Its lone moon's orbit was likely disrupted by the testing, as well.<ref name="BSOTEAFO" />

==History==
{{Quote|Why would someone do this?''"<br />"''Patience, kid. That's what we're gonna find out.|Kazuda Xiono and Poe Dameron|audio=KazWhyWouldSomeoneDoThis-TheCoreProblem.flac|<ref name="The Core Problem" />}}
During the [[Cold War]] between the First Order and the [[New Republic]]-funded [[Resistance]],<ref name="The Core Problem" /> the planets and celestial bodies of the Dassal system were located in the First Order's Sector Epsilon 51-3.<ref name="Descent">{{Resistance|Descent (episode)}}</ref> They were cored out by the First Order<ref name="The Core Problem" /> as tests for the construction of the [[Starkiller Base]] [[superweapon]],<ref name="Resistance Rewind" /> which also caused the disappearance of the system's [[Star|sun]].<ref name="The Core Problem" /> Unlike the other celestial bodies in the system, which cracked and broke apart, the First Order's third attempt, using Najra-Va,<ref name="Resistance Rewind" /> left the planet largely intact save for the massive hole that had been [[Mining|mined]] through its core,<ref name="The Core Problem" /> likely due to a reduced power level during testing to calculate Starkiller Base's limits.<ref name="BSOTEAFO" />

[[File:IntoNajraVa-TheCoreProblem.jpg|thumb|left|270px|The planet after having its core drilled through by the First Order]]
After retrieving intelligence from the First Order<ref name="The Core Problem" /> in [[34 ABY]],<ref name="TCP Date">{{ResistanceDate|1|17}}</ref> the Resistance [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] learned of its activity in the Dassal system. Informing fellow Resistance member [[Poe Dameron]], the two [[Resistance pilot|pilots]] then [[Mission to the Dassal system|investigated]] the system. Discovering the cored and broken celestial bodies, they came across Najra-Va and flew through its core. The [[pilot]]s almost crashed their [[starship]]s due to the planet's intact [[gravity]] well but managed to escape through the other side of Najra-Va, landing on its [[moon]]. Once the First Order was alerted to their presence by a [[Spider probe droid|probe droid]], Dameron and Xiono were chased back into Najra-Va's core by several [[TIE/fo space superiority fighter|TIE fighters]] led by First Order [[Major]] [[Elrik Vonreg]]. The Resistance pilots used the gravity well to their advantage, causing the enemy [[Starfighter|fighters]] to crash, which forced Vonreg to retreat and allowed the pair to escape.<ref name="The Core Problem" />

==Inhabitants==
The Dassal system, which included Najra-Va, was once thriving with life.<ref name="Databank" /> However, all of Najra-Va's inhabitants were [[Death|killed]] when the First Order experimented on the system.<ref name="BSOTEAFO" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|&hellip;the fun stuff around The Core Problem [&hellip;] flying through the gravity wells inside the cored out planet. It gave us an opportunity to kind of be doing something that was super relevant and super tied in to what was happening in the movies, but also kind of do our own unique stuff that you don't get to see anywhere else.|Chris "Doc" Wyatt about Najra-Va, when asked about his favorite scene written from ''Star Wars Resistance''|audio=NajraVa-ChrisWyatt.flac|<ref name="WookInterview">{{WookYouTube|video=c-i_MhMIFnA|text=Wookieepedia Interviews - Doc Wyatt & Chris Burke}}</ref>}}
Najra-Va first appeared in "[[The Core Problem]],"<ref name="The Core Problem" /> the seventeenth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'',<ref name="Insider 190">{{InsiderCite|190|Resistance Revisited|''Resistance'' Revisited}}</ref> which aired on [[February 17]], [[2019]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> However, one of the shots with Najra-Va was included in the mid-season trailer for the show, which was uploaded to [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] on [[January 9]] of that year.<ref name="Mid-season">{{SWYouTube|m7Pls-vYWwM|Star Wars Resistance Season 1 - Mid-Season Trailer (Official)|sw_url=video/season-1-mid-season-trailer-star-wars-resistance}}</ref>

[[File:NajraVa-ConceptArt.png|thumb|right|270px|Concept art of the planet's core shaft]]
One of the writers of "The Core Problem," [[Chris "Doc" Wyatt]], felt that the scene in which Xiono and Dameron flew through Najra-Va was among the favorite moments they had written for ''Star Wars Resistance''. Wyatt and the episode's other writer, [[Kevin Burke]], felt that viewers of the show who had seen<ref name="WookInterview" /> the [[2015]] [[sequel trilogy]] film<ref name="TFA">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']],<ref name="WookInterview" /> in which Starkiller Base&mdash;a [[superweapon]] made from the cored-out planet [[Ilum]]<ref name="TFA" />&mdash;would find Najra-Va interesting, as it was an early by the First Order to drill through a planet using the base. The pair considered the episode visually stunning, praising the installment in that it felt like a seamless cutscene from ''The Force Awakens'' due to its connection of Ilum and Najra-Va, conceptually.<ref name="WookInterview" />

Concept artwork for the planet's core shaft was created by [[Lucasfilm Animation]] artist [[Jim Moore]] on [[August 28]], [[2017]].<ref name="Concept art">{{SW|url=star-wars-resistance-the-core-program-concept-art-gallery|text="The Core Problem" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 9}}</ref> The planet's name was identified in the [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry for the Dassal system.<ref name="Databank" /> While several sources refer to Najra-Va as a planetoid,<ref name="BXW87">{{BuildXWingCite|87|Starfighter Aces}}</ref><ref name="Bucket's List TCP">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-core-problem-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 7 Fun Facts from "The Core Problem" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref> several other sources refer to it as a planet.<ref name="Databank" /><ref name="BSOTEAFO" /><ref name="TR">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Resistance}}</ref> This article conforms to the majority of newer sources in regards to the contradiction and considers Najra-Va a planet.

